module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionExtension.Ample
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionExtension.Consumers
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleAffineAvoidance.AmpleFiniteSet

/-!
# What the ample case of Stacks Tag 01PW discharges

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionExtension/Ample.lean` proves
`Stacks.SectionExtension.IsSectionRatio X L` — the surjectivity half of Stacks Tag 01PW — whenever
`L` is **ample**. `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionExtension/Consumers.lean` had already
reduced the ample cluster to that predicate. This file composes the two, so that every statement
whose only remaining hypothesis was the section-extension premise *for an ample module* becomes
unconditional.

Which statements those are is decided by one question: is the module the premise is applied to
known to be ample at the point of use? Where it is, the hypothesis goes away. Where the ampleness
of that module is the *conclusion*, it does not; see "What is not done".

## Main results

* `Stacks.SectionExtension.isBasisNonvanishing_of_isAmple` and
  `Stacks.SectionExtension.isBasisAffineNonvanishing_of_isAmple`: **clauses (3) and (4) of Stacks
  Tag 01Q3 from clause (1), unconditionally.** For `L` ample the opens `X_s` — respectively the
  affine ones among them — form a basis for the topology of `X`.
* `Stacks.SectionExtension.isAmple_iff_compactSpace_and_isBasisNonvanishing` and
  `Stacks.SectionExtension.isAmple_iff_compactSpace_and_isBasisAffineNonvanishing`: the
  three-way equivalence (1) ⟺ (3) ⟺ (4), with no premise, for an arbitrary invertible module.
* `Stacks.SectionExtension.basicOpenIsPow_of_isAmple`:
  `Stacks.AmpleQuasiAffinePullback.BasicOpenIsPow` for an ample module — every basic open of an
  `X_s` is itself an `X_u`, with no affineness hypothesis on `X_s`.
* `Stacks.SectionExtension.isAmple_pullbackModule`: **Stacks Tag 0B3E in general**, with no
  premise: the pullback of an ample module along a quasi-compact immersion (or embedding, or along
  any immersion of a quasi-compact scheme) is ample.
* `Stacks.SectionExtension.amplePullbackGap`: `Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.AmplePullbackGap` is a
  theorem, and with it
  `Stacks.SectionExtension.isRelativelyAmple_of_relativeTwistImmersion`, the content of Stacks Tag
  01VN.
* `Stacks.SectionExtension.exists_affine_nvOpen_containing_finite_le_of_isAmple`: **the conclusion
  of Stacks Tag 09NV, with no premise.** A finite subset of an open `W` of a scheme carrying an
  ample invertible module lies in an affine `X_a ≤ W`.

## No Stacks attribute is attached

Three labels are at stake and none of the three has its covering set here.

* **01PW** is proved only for an ample `L`, and only in the `𝓕 = 𝒪_X`, surjectivity half; see the
  module documentation of `Stacks.SectionExtension.Ample`.
* **01Q3** asserts the equivalence of all nine of its clauses. What is proved is
  (1) ⟺ (3) ⟺ (4). Clause (2) — the immersion into `Proj Γ_*(X, L)` — and clauses (5) to (9) are
  untouched; clause (7) is discussed below.
* **09NV** is the label of another statement, and
  `Stacks.AmpleAffineAvoidance.exists_affine_nvOpen_containing_finite_le_of_ample` already records
  that. What changes here is only that its one hypothesis is discharged.

Stacks Tag 0B3E's attribute already sits on `Stacks.AmplePullback.isAmple_modulePullback`, and
Stacks Tag 01VN's on the `Stacks.Tag01VN` declarations, both carrying the premise; the declarations
below discharge it rather than restate those labels.

## What is not done

**Part (2) of Stacks Tag 0892 is not closed, and the obstruction is circularity, not generality.**
`Stacks.AmpleQuasiAffinePullback.isAmple_modulePullback_of_isQuasiAffineHom` applies
`Stacks.AmpleQuasiAffinePullback.BasicOpenIsPow X (f^* M)` — the premise for the *pulled-back*
module on `X` — and the only ampleness in its hypotheses is `IsAmple S M`, downstairs. `IsAmple X
(f^* M)` is that theorem's conclusion, so `basicOpenIsPow_of_isAmple` instantiated there would
require exactly what is being proved. Discharging it needs Tag 01PW for an invertible module that
is *not* assumed ample — the generality `Stacks.SectionExtension.IsSectionRatio` is stated in and
that `Stacks.SectionExtension.Ample` does not reach.

**Clause (7) of Stacks Tag 01Q3 is not closed either, and nothing here is on its path.** The
residual recorded at `Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_clauseFive` is clause
(5): for every positive `d` and every `j`, some tensor power of `L ^⊗ d` twists `L ^⊗ j` into a
module generated by finitely many global sections. Clause (5) is the **module-valued** form of Tag
01PW, about an arbitrary quasi-coherent `𝓕`; `Stacks.SectionExtension.IsSectionRatio` is the case
`𝓕 = 𝒪_X` and no declaration in this repository derives one from the other. So the two halves of
clause (7) that Stacks Tags 0EBD and 087S were said to wait on are *not* unblocked by the ample
case of 01PW.

